\f1\fs22 Around midmorning on the next day, The High Elvis arrived in his parliamentary convertible.\
\pard\pardeftab720\fi360\sl220\qj\partightenfactor0

\f0\fs24 \cf2 \expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
<!$Scr_Ps::0><$Scr_Ps::1>
\f1\fs22 If his temper had soured at the first checkpoint, he was less than equanimous by the time he was told only approved vehicles were permitted on the road to the compound gates.\
\'93Hey, I\'92m an entertainer, I\'92ve come to visit the Holy Momma.\'94\
\'93Well, perhaps you can entertain your dear mum from here,\'94 he was told.\
The High Elvis turned the engine off.\
\'93We must ask you to clear the checkpoint,\'94 he was told.\
The High Elvis pulled out his device and called the Holy Momma.\
Sarah answered warily and received a quick yet comprehensive account of the UDF occupation of the village and the final roadblock preventing the High Elvis from attending her. \
She tried not to betray her shock when she answered. \'93I cannot order the military around, High Elvis.\'94\
The High Elvis thought for a moment. \'93Are you safe?\'94\
\'93Yes,\'94 Sarah answered, hoping there would not be more questions. \'93Aunt Kathy tells me Little Clinton will be arriving soon, and I must rest up.\'94\
\'93Very well, Holy Momma,\'94 the High Elvis conceded. \'93We will be with you in time for the birth.\'94\
\pard\pardeftab720\sl220\sb220\qj\partightenfactor0

\f0\fs24 \cf2 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 <!$Scr_Ps::1><$Scr_Ps::0>
\f1\fs22 The High Elvis called his fellow clone descendants to the compound gate. Hundreds of Elvi arrived within minutes, many bringing guitar cases, and together they marched the last section of the road to the gate. The troops watched warily, and when it seemed the Elvi might attempt to stride right through the membrane, one shouted out, \'93Hey! You\'92ll get yourselves killed.\'94\
\pard\pardeftab720\fi360\sl220\qj\partightenfactor0

\f0\fs24 \cf2 \expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
<!$Scr_Ps::0><$Scr_Ps::1>
\f1\fs22 But the High Elvi had no attention of trying to walk through. The way the membrane distorted and clouded everything beyond gave more than enough pause. He did however walk a little too close, and saw the violet vertical lights glow up. Unfortunately, the headstock end of his case passed into the membrane. The violet bars flashed and, with nothing as loud as a fizzle, swiftly beheaded his second-favorite guitar.
\f0\fs24 <!$Scr_Ps::1>}